From 202bef515040f79df9c78af1ac48586bbb50daef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:29:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wip(cd26): pinned place sites, unfinished [skip ci]

A pinned place point (an at site, the core centre) is held 0.1 border
units inside its place: exact bisector check, a capacity-constrained
Lloyd hold for at pins, and a core heart (a disc of its share round the
centre, the others angular wedges round it) where no power cell can hold
the centre. Four K7 drafts use it; docs, schema and skills describe the
core heart.

Proven: before the last change the full build was green (1368 tests)
with goldens unchanged. Unproven: the last change, generalising the heart
to any single at pin (hub index, off-centre wedges) to cure the K6
the_sunken_temple regression (a 50% place pinned at the centre refused by
the margin). It compiles; PlaceLayoutTest was stopped before it finished.
State and next steps: mods/custom-dimensions-26/fidelity/drafts/k8/STATE.md.

