+# K8 state: pinned place sites (small heart) — unfinished
+
+Worktree: /home/user/minecraft-server-template/.claude/worktrees/agent-a71605a46a7f6758a, branch worktree-agent-a71605a46a7f6758a (forked from claude/minecraft-dependency-automation-n1w79q at 8719275e; that branch has since moved, to b66da114 or later: rebase before the final build). Brief: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/5eb91d81-f3fb-5a91-9f20-35496482f7d0/scratchpad/k8-brief.md (common rules beside it). Log: progress.log beside this file.
+
+## The finding that shaped the design
+A convex cell clear of a disc of radius m round the centre holds at most (1 − m)/2 of the square. So no power diagram keeps a small place at the centre beside a neighbour of 45% or more, whatever the solver does (moving free sites outwards, sectors rings, capacity-constrained Lloyd were all tried and fail on 20/50/15/15). The K7 cases (neighbours of 50, 51, 52, 55%) are impossible with convex cells.
+
+## Design as built
+- `PlaceField.PIN_MARGIN` = 0.1 border units: a pinned point must lie that far inside its place. `reach(a, i, u, v, margin)` measures it exactly from the power bisectors; `unheld(a, anchors)`.
+- `hold(a, target, anchors, grid)`: for `at` pins, if a pin does not hold, a capacity-constrained Lloyd iteration (pinned site moves by centroid→pin gap, free sites half-way to centroid, weights re-solved, 30 rounds). Used in the auto search (`search`) and after `refine`, and for all-`at` definitions. Returns `a` unchanged when every pin holds (so goldens do not move).
+- Heart: `Arrangement` gains `heart` (radius), `wedges` (compass bearings) and `hub` (the heart's place index). The hub place is the disc of area = its share (r = √(4 share/π)) round its point; the others are angular wedges from that point clockwise in list order, the first centred on `direction`, bearings integrated (`wedges(...)`, 36,000 steps, reach from the point to the square edge) so each wedge holds its share of the square less the disc. Every wedge meets the heart and reaches the border.
+- DF encoding (compile `least`): heart term `floor(clamp(|p−c|²/r², 0, 1)) × (2^24 − 16) (+ hub)`, wedge term `floor(clamp(−m × 2^20, 0, 1)) × (2^24 − 16) + place`, m = min (span ≤ 180°) or max of the signed distances to the two rays. Node types are the existing ones (add, mul, square, clamp, floor, min, max): T217 shape unchanged in kind, only new constants/terms; no new boot check.
+- Where it applies (PlaceLayout.build): `core` solves its even ring first and keeps it when the centre holds (every core whose first place is its largest: places_core golden unchanged); otherwise `PlaceField.heart(shares, 0, 0, 0, direction)`, refused with "the core arrangement cannot keep X (s%) at the centre with N blocks round it…" when the heart is narrower than the margin or one region check fails. `ring`, `sectors`, `bands` sites are not pinned. All-`at`: Lloyd hold, else refused naming the place and the place that reaches over it. Auto with `at` pins: search+hold; if nothing holds and exactly ONE place is pinned, that place becomes a heart at its site (hub ≠ 0 possible) — this is the fix in progress; else refused.
+
+## Status
+- Committed as wip (see git log). Build: the whole tree built green with 1368 tests (core 712, compiler 541, server 115; head had 1362) and goldens unchanged BEFORE the last change (the hub generalisation in edit4: `hub` field, off-centre wedges, single-pin heart fallback, test `aLonePinNoPowerCellCanHoldBecomesAHeartAtItsSite`). That last change compiled far enough to start `:compiler:test --tests '*PlaceLayoutTest*'`, which was stopped unfinished: UNPROVEN.
+- Regression being fixed: K6 draft `fidelity/drafts/k6/the_sunken_temple.json` (two places 50/50, `at` highlands [0, 0]) was refused by the margin; the single-pin heart should cure it (a 50% disc r = 0.8 at the centre fits inside 1 − 0.1). Re-run the land harness to confirm.
+- Drafts updated and sampled with the pre-hub code (/tmp/claude-0/k8/dbg/four.txt; 128-cell grid, seed 20261022): the_teal_corruption (new; core, warped first, zone removed) 20.5/50.2/12.0/11.2/6.2, spawn 658 blocks inside the heart; the_gilded_pit (core, blackstone_basin heart) 20.5/50.1/20.3/9.0, spawn 210 inside; the_forged_depths (core, quartz_flats moved first so forge is the heart) 20.5/55.2/24.3, spawn 273 inside; the_emberglass_foundry (`at` columns at spawn [-128, 128]) 11.2/16.7/53.0/19.1, spawn 35 inside (margin 26). The other 31 K7 drafts' shares are identical to K7's compile-final.log. README rows updated.
+- Docs edited: worldgen.md places paragraph, placeness.md, schema descriptions (`arrangement`, `at`), both cutover skills (worldgen-tuning, custom-dimension-authoring). They describe core's heart; they do NOT yet mention the single-`at` heart fallback.
+- Goldens/fixtures: none change (places_core's first place is its largest, so its even ring holds).
+
+## Remaining steps, in order
+1. Run `:compiler:test --tests '*PlaceLayoutTest*'`; fix failures in the hub change (wedge order, `other(j)`, heart bounds check, test expectations).
+2. Re-run the K7 harness on k7 and k6 drafts and the land harness; confirm the_sunken_temple compiles and its highlands hold the centre.
+3. Add the single-pin heart to worldgen.md / placeness.md / schema `at` description; then `./cutover/mkshas.sh` and a clean-clone `./cutover/apply.sh --dry-run` (no `!` line).
+4. Rebase on the branch head, full build (compare test count with /tmp/claude-0/w10c1r/progress.log), quick gate `PATH=/tmp/claude-0/pybin:/root/.local/bin:/tmp/claude-0/sc/bin:$PATH ./scripts/test-scripts.sh --quick`, commit with explicit paths and `[skip ci]`.
+5. Write /tmp/claude-0/k8/land-shares.md (notes below) and the report, with trap draft T259 (a power cell need not contain its site; a convex cell clear of a centred disc of m holds at most (1−m)/2; a small heart is a disc + wedges).
+
+## Commands
+- Java: `export JAVA_HOME=/home/user/.local/jdk/jdk-25.0.5+8 PATH=/home/user/.local/jdk/jdk-25.0.5+8/bin:$PATH`; check `free -g` ≥ 5 GB available.
+- From mods/custom-dimensions-26: `./gradlew --max-workers=1 --offline :compiler:test --tests '*PlaceLayoutTest*'` (~2 min), `./gradlew --max-workers=1 --offline build` (~3 min). Vanilla data must be copied into compiler/build/vanilla/26.3 from the main checkout (read-only) in a fresh worktree.
+- Failures: `python3 /tmp/claude-0/k8/scratch/fails.py` (reads compiler/build/test-results/test).
+- K7 harness (samples each draft's compiled field, prints shares, regions, spawn place and its edge distance): `bash /tmp/claude-0/k8/dbg/run.sh <drafts dir>` (needs the compiled test classes; source /tmp/claude-0/k8/dbg/src/.../K7Drafts.java).
+- Land harness (border share vs land share per place over 5 seeds): `bash /tmp/claude-0/k8/dbg/land.sh the_aviary the_sunken_temple the_violet_spire the_burning_archipelago the_shattered_skies` (source K8Land.java; compiles definitions + k6 + k7 drafts).
+- Scratch solver probe: `bash /tmp/claude-0/k8/scratch/run.sh` (Heart.java).
+
+## Land shares write-up (notes, not yet measured)
+- Precedent: `customdimensions:land_share` (server/.../zone/LandShareFunction) measures the seed's own noise when the router compiles (96×96 grid) and shifts continentalness. A place field could do the same: a custom DF type that, at compileSampler, samples the terrain's land cue (`<prefix>/place` > 0, the router's continents on void terrains) on a grid and re-solves the weights against the land mask. Roller and server agree because both compile the router for the seed through the same code. Cost per rolled seed: ~16k cue samples plus a weight solve (n × 16k × ≤400), roughly 0.1–0.2 s. Downsides: a new DF type (T217 shape change and a boot check), weights no longer in the datapack, a step-function objective on sparse islands (an edge through an island splits it; tolerance must follow island granularity), and the 4 × 8 seed-chosen layouts re-solved per seed.
+- Cheaper compile-time alternative: solve against the expected land density (the islands noise's known spread plus `terrain.layout`'s deterministic shape, via Noises.threshold), seed-free, which removes the systematic bias of `radial` clusters (most of a cell in empty sky) but not per-seed scatter.
+- Candidate users: the_aviary, the_sunken_temple, the_violet_spire, the_burning_archipelago (End coverage 0.04: few islands, scatter dominates), the_shattered_skies. K7's recipe for a radial cluster remains `sectors`. Measure the gap with the land harness before deciding.
